Here is an example of a basic todo list component in React:

**TodoList.js**
```jsx
import React, { useState } from 'react';

function TodoList() {
  const [todos, setTodos] = useState([]);
  const [newTodo, setNewTodo] = useState('');

  const handleSubmit = (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    setTodos([...todos, { task: newTodo, completed: false }]);
    setNewTodo('');
  };

  const handleToggle = (index) => {
    setTodos(
      todos.map((todo, i) => (
        i === index ? { ...todo, completed: !todo.completed } : todo
      ))
    );
  };

  const handleDelete = (index) => {
    setTodos(todos.filter((todo, i) => i !== index));
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
        <input
          type="text"
          value={newTodo}
          onChange={(event) => setNewTodo(event.target.value)}
          placeholder="Enter new todo..."
        />
        <button type="submit">Add Todo</button>
      </form>
      <ul>
        {todos.map((todo, index) => (
          <li key={index}>
            <input
              type="checkbox"
              checked={todo.completed}
              onClick={() => handleToggle(index)}
            />
            <span style={{ textDecoration: todo.completed ? 'line-through' : 'none' }}>
              {todo.task}
            </span>
            <button onClick={() => handleDelete(index)}>X</button>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  );
}

export default TodoList;
```
Let me explain what's going on:

* We use the `useState` hook to store the todo list and the new todo input value in state variables `todos` and `newTodo`, respectively.
* We define three functions:
	+ `handleSubmit`: triggered when the user submits the form. It adds the new todo to the list and clears the input field.
	+ `handleToggle`: toggles the completion status of a todo item.
	+ `handleDelete`: removes a todo item from the list.
* We use the `map` method to render the todo list items. Each item consists of:
	+ A checkbox to toggle completion status
	+ The todo task text with a line-through decoration if completed
	+ A deletion button to remove the item

